
ESP32 DS18B20 Temperature Reader
https://cdn.sparkfun.com/datasheets/Sensors/Temp/DS18B20.pdf
================================

This small PlatformIO project reads temperature data from a DS18B20
one-wire temperature sensor using an ESP32 board. It uses the
OneWire and DallasTemperature libraries to request and print
temperature readings to the serial monitor every 2 seconds.

Hardware
--------
- ESP32 development board (example: YD-ESP32-S3)
- DS18B20 one-wire temperature sensor
- 4.7k Ohm pull-up resistor between Data and 3.3V

Wiring
-------
- DS18B20 Data pin -> GPIO4 on the ESP32
- DS18B20 VCC -> 3.3V
- DS18B20 GND -> GND
- 4.7k resistor between Data and 3.3V (required for reliable bus operation)

Software / Libraries
--------------------
- PlatformIO (recommended) or Arduino framework for ESP32
- Libraries used:
	- OneWire
	- DallasTemperature

Build and Upload
----------------
Use PlatformIO in VS Code or the CLI:

- Build: `pio run`
- Upload: `pio run -t upload`
- Monitor serial output: `pio device monitor -b 115200`

Usage
-----
1. Connect the hardware as described above.
2. Build and upload the firmware to your ESP32.
3. Open the serial monitor at 115200 baud to view temperature readings.

Example Output
--------------
DS18B20 Temperature Sensor Test
Found 1 sensor(s).
Requesting temperatures...DONE
Temperature for Device 1: 24.50 °C

Troubleshooting
---------------
- If no sensor is detected, check wiring and ensure the 4.7k pull-up is present.
- Verify the correct GPIO pin is used and matches `src/main.cpp` (currently GPIO4).
